From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@zoho.eu>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 18:43:48 +0300
Subject: OpenGL 2: sprites as a 2D atlas instead of a 3D texture

Without array textures the game used GL_TEXTURE_3D, which the PS3's GPU takes only
up to 512 and which Mesa's texture compression patch does not touch. The frames go
into one GL_TEXTURE_2D now: a grid, as many columns as fit the width, power-of-two
size (at most 4096), transparent padding; frames are halved if they do not fit.
Sprite::Atlas() gives the shaders the cell size and half a texel, the sprite,
batch and outline shaders take it as the uniform 'atlas' (the sprite shader a second
one, 'maskAtlas', for the swizzle mask). The array texture path is unchanged.

